  "authoringNote": "The one current usable order is final and states the beneficiary name and identifier, the order date, item description, quantity and treating practitioner, but its signature is null, so R03 holds element_missing for element.signature on that order (SPEC R03 and F03; pack R03 missing outcome). The finding is missing for the authorization coordinator, whose remedy is to request the existing signed order; the oracle never fills, generates or authenticates a signature. R03 cites the seven stated element facts; the null signer name and signed date are not facts and are not cited. A missing finding names no parent document (C07); the condition names the order. R04 does not read signature metadata: the final encounter (2026-08-20) and final order (2026-09-02) share SYN-PRAC-0001 and the order is within the C01 bound 2027-02-20, so R04 passes with six citations. The receipt references the order and states 2026-09-03T17:05:00Z, after the C06 span 2026-09-01T10:00Z to 2026-09-03T12:00Z, so R05 passes with four citations. R01 passes (seven supplier fields and the order code), R02 passes (six beneficiary facts), R06 is qualified clinical review citing five clinical statements with no administrative effect, R07 passes citing the false LCMP flag, R08 and R09 pass and R10 is not applicable. The highest effect is needs_information. Distinct from F03x1 (a complete order beside one lacking signature) and F03x2 (signer names differ).",
